c.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation checkpoint: commit 8a87dff27851dfae89526b3dff59b4d077deab6c (Change-Id I1d2270be824fa4154ca1bae6f336697651b14380) changes exactly the four declared paths and only the 13 allowlisted comments/docstrings. Author-side oracle PASS: 13/13 blocks shrink, 1,223 -> 409 words; immutable-base AST/runtime, every non-allowlisted comment token, directives, and shebangs are unchanged. Focused IO/contract tests: 30 passed in 55.53s. Comment hygiene, diff-check, make lint, DCO/message hooks, and verify-commit-ticket all pass. Per operator instruction for this documentation-only epic, the full local make verify was intentionally not run; Gerrit CI will provide the full gate. Independent non-author 13-row TSV review remains required before closure.","timestamp":1788820402453776104},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed commit 8a87dff27851 as Gerrit change 2803: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2803. Tagged rebar-session-59a7-cb88. Awaiting LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and independent 13-row TSV review before submit/close.","timestamp":1788820458969280944}],"created_at":1788570779866207238,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"27dcf27e-ca99-4533-ba84-f25dbdd7d44e","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"6ce6-9ee8-629c-457b"},{"link_uuid":"b9149cfe-baaa-47c4-8da1-6b598890d23c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"3cba-e13e-3d1a-4e9e"},{"link_uuid":"647ce8a3-1eb3-438f-b79c-a45291c1f585","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"def8-f8f1-6e79-418d"},{"link_uuid":"43158ed7-cb86-467f-8440-5139c3c39a15","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"80b0-e372-308b-49ac"},{"link_uuid":"f54faa6b-30a1-46e9-b578-25c76d59e04c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0d26-c296-0334-41af"}],"description":"## Context / immutable audit base\nAt d49fea41cc383dc70d465903e94598a6dc790bd1, these four files contain 13 confirmed prose blocks that can be condensed without behavior change. The former older-SHA ranges mixed prose and code and missed four long owner docstrings/comments. Lines are immutable-base citations, not edit coordinates.\n\n## Exact prose allowlist\nA stable ID is the full path plus :: plus the listed suffix. Only these blocks may change.\n\n- src/rebar/_io/_cli.py (3): module-docstring@1-7; export_cli::comment(The factory is the parser of record)@29-37; import_cli::comment(Factory is the parser of record)@102-106.\n- src/rebar/_io/_provenance.py (3): module-docstring@1-8; _coerce_ns-docstring@16-25; create_kwargs-docstring@35-45.\n- src/rebar/_io/_strip.py (1): module-docstring@1-15.\n- src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py (6): module-docstring@1-39; _scan_existing_source_ids-docstring@93-97; import_tickets-docstring@123-134; import_tickets::comment(Chunk size for the batched-commit flush)@184-189; import_tickets::comment(transition_core requires a bounded class)@356-361; import_tickets::comment(Every closeable ticket is still open here)@370-376.\n\n## Contracts, consumers, and exclusions\nPreserve the argparse-inexpressible token rules and error/output channels; exact nanosecond coercion; source-versus-local-genesis provenance; provider key/comment-id stripping while retaining source_* fields; two-pass/sub-phase ordering; source_id idempotence; chunk boundaries; deferred push; children-before-parents; and the ordinary-close/no-force invariant. Real consumers are export/import CLI handlers and the locked write/reducer paths; no allowlisted docstring is read via __doc__ or inspect.getdoc in the audited tree.\n\nAll non-allowlisted prose and all runtime strings, assertions, fixtures, decorators, subprocess arguments, config values/keys, directives, and shebangs remain byte-identical. Preserve _cli.py T201 directives at lines 66/67/86/116/117/123/124/137/139; import_ndjson.py read-via directives at 216/217/395 and BLE001 directives at 290/306/312/330/348/353/385.\n\n## Verification and independent review\nParse base/final Python with type_comments=True; strip only allowlisted owner docstrings, normalize only ast.TypeIgnore.lineno, and require remaining AST/runtime equality. Require directive/shebang physical-line equality and exact HEAD^..HEAD paths. Run focused IO contracts, path diff-check, hygiene, and untimed worktree-venv make verify.\n\nA non-author reviewer records a leaf-linked TSV with exactly 13 PASS rows: stable_id, before_citation, final_citation, preserved_contract_or_consumer, directives_exact, before_words, final_words, reviewer_session, semantic_pass, bloat_pass. Every block must shrink; missing/extra/FAIL rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly the 13 allowlisted blocks are shortened; no other prose or directive changes.\n- [ ] The immutable AST/runtime and directive oracle passes for all four files.\n- [ ] Every listed parsing, provenance, stripping, ordering, batching, and close contract has an independent-review PASS citation.\n- [ ] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the four declared paths; focused checks, diff-check, hygiene, and make verify exit 0.\n- [ ] The independent TSV has exactly 13 complete PASS rows with lower final word counts.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_io/_cli.py","reason":"Condense only 3 audited export/import parser prose blocks while preserving argparse-inexpressible token behavior, output channels, and T201 directives."},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/_provenance.py","reason":"Condense only 3 audited provenance docstrings while preserving exact nanosecond coercion and source-versus-local-genesis semantics."},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/_strip.py","reason":"Condense only the audited module docstring while preserving provider key/comment-id stripping and source_* retention."},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py","reason":"Condense only 6 audited import, batching, and close prose blocks while preserving pass order, idempotence, chunking, ordinary-close authority, env controls, and directives."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6"],["relates_to","0d26-c296-0334-41af"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"d6eb-1c6c-88c3-48f6","parent_status_uuid":"a36414bc-29a7-4408-ac17-f4f4df7e8def","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"ad60-37a0-2d1d-4688","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in src/rebar/_io","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c '\nimport ast, io, subprocess, tokenize\nfrom pathlib import Path\nB = \"d49fea41cc383dc70d465903e94598a6dc790bd1\"\nA = {\"src/rebar/_io/_cli.py\":[\"module\"],\"src/rebar/_io/_provenance.py\":[\"module\",\"_coerce_ns\",\"create_kwargs\"],\"src/rebar/_io/_strip.py\":[\"module\"],\"src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py\":[\"module\",\"_scan_existing_source_ids\",\"import_tickets\"]}\nTOKENS = (\"noqa\", \"type:\", \"pyright:\", \"mypy:\", \"ruff:\", \"fmt:\", \"isort:\", \"pragma:\", \"nosec\", \"coverage:\", \"mechanism-ok:\", \"raw-git-ok:\", \"tickets-boundary-ok:\", \"read-via:\")\ndef normalize(src, path):\n    tree = ast.parse(src, filename=path, type_comments=True)\n    def visit(node, prefix=\"\"):\n        owner = \"module\" if isinstance(node, ast.Module) else prefix\n        body = getattr(node, \"body\", [])\n        if owner in A[path] and body and isinstance(body[0], ast.Expr) and isinstance(body[0].value, ast.Constant) and isinstance(body[0].value.value, str):\n            body[0].value.value = \"__ALLOWLISTED_PROSE__\"\n        for child in body:\n            if isinstance(child, (ast.ClassDef, ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)):\n                qualified = f\"{prefix}.{child.name}\" if prefix else child.name\n                visit(child, qualified)\n    visit(tree)\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(node, ast.TypeIgnore):\n            node.lineno = 0\n    return ast.dump(tree, include_attributes=False)\ndef directives(src):\n    lines = src.splitlines()\n    found = []\n    for tok in tokenize.generate_tokens(io.StringIO(src).readline):\n        if tok.type != tokenize.COMMENT:\n            continue\n        body = tok.string[1:].lstrip()\n        if tok.string.startswith(\"#!\") or any(body.startswith(prefix) for prefix in TOKENS):\n            found.append(lines[tok.start[0] - 1])\n    return found\nfor path in A:\n    before = subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", f\"{B}:{path}\"], text=True)\n    final = Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    assert normalize(before, path) == normalize(final, path), (\"AST/runtime drift\", path)\n    assert directives(before) == directives(final), (\"directive/shebang drift\", path)\n'","dd_id":"immutable-prose-only","dd_text":"Only allowlisted prose may change; after stripping those owner docstrings, base and final AST/runtime trees match, with only TypeIgnore.lineno normalized, and directive/shebang physical lines are identical."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'import subprocess; expected=set([\"src/rebar/_io/_cli.py\",\"src/rebar/_io/_provenance.py\",\"src/rebar/_io/_strip.py\",\"src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py\"]); actual=set(subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"diff\",\"--name-only\",\"HEAD^..HEAD\"],text=True).splitlines()); assert actual==expected,{\"expected\":sorted(expected),\"actual\":sorted(actual)}'","dd_id":"exact-leaf-paths","dd_text":"The single ticket commit changes exactly the declared file-impact set."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","dd_id":"comment-hygiene","dd_text":"The repository comment-hygiene policy passes."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest -q tests/interfaces/io/test_export_ndjson.py tests/interfaces/io/test_import_ndjson.py tests/unit/io/test_strip_external.py tests/unit/test_c3b_push_defer_coupling_heldout.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_operation_snapshot_authoritative_binding.py","dd_id":"focused-contracts","dd_text":"Focused tests for every preserved subsystem contract pass."},{"command":"rtk git diff --check HEAD^..HEAD -- src/rebar/_io/_cli.py src/rebar/_io/_provenance.py src/rebar/_io/_strip.py src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py","dd_id":"diff-integrity","dd_text":"The path-scoped patch contains no whitespace errors."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify","dd_id":"repository-gates","dd_text":"The complete local CI contract passes in the worktree virtualenv; do not apply a timeout."}]},"source_event_uuids":["a84d6123-b9ba-4169-9a41-eb61c75c2512","fb104446-0338-458b-8b02-147d2c5fc280","4396e145-8d08-4178-a8a5-d3ae1184044a","0dde74c6-2d79-46ac-a859-46b05f1750bf","fce30a0a-4ce5-41c8-b788-c68e917326cb","31ba2f90-cce2-4272-8863-a907a3ab9415","715b344f-6b40-4776-a5a6-8234aa735884","a36414bc-29a7-4408-ac17-f4f4df7e8def","1f83bec5-90a2-41bc-8aa2-cc90f74b19a4","f5fe614a-cff3-495e-8cb6-819e8b2073c4","e4b9cb29-f981-464d-89f9-0ac1e38e0013","f54faa6b-30a1-46e9-b578-25c76d59e04c"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788827365003131282,"uuid":"ea7fc0a4-6cb9-4d30-ada0-4b0db5f89937"}